# Copy to `.env` and fill in. Client-safe, PUBLIC identifiers only — no
# secrets belong in any VITE_ var, because Vite inlines them into the browser
# bundle at build time. Anything here ships to every visitor.
#
# Server-side secrets (SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, ORACLE_AUTHORITY_PRIVATE_KEY,
# DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY, ADMIN_PRIVATE_KEY) are deliberately NOT listed here.
# See "Server-side secrets" at the bottom for where those actually go.

# --- Shared market feed (Supabase / Lovable Cloud) ---------------------------
# Both values are public. RLS (supabase/migrations/0001_market_state.sql) gives
# this key read-only access to market data and nothing else — it cannot write a
# price or forge a chart point.
#
# NOTE the key name: it is PUBLISHABLE, not ANON. Supabase's newer opaque key
# format renamed it, and src/integrations/supabase/client.ts (generated and
# owned by Lovable Cloud) reads VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY. Setting
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY instead leaves the client unconfigured, and the app
# silently falls back to opening prices with a flat chart rather than erroring
# — so the mistake is easy to miss. Find both under Supabase → Project
# Settings → API.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# --- Robinhood Chain ---------------------------------------------------------
# "testnet" (chain id 46630) or "mainnet" (chain id 4663). Defaults to testnet
# when unset, so a missing var can never silently point the app at mainnet with
# real funds — see src/lib/evm/chain.ts.
VITE_ROBINHOOD_NETWORK=testnet
VITE_ROBINHOOD_RPC_URL=https://rpc.testnet.chain.robinhood.com

# The deployed SharpsMarket contract (evm/src/SharpsMarket.sol), from the
# `forge script Deploy` output. While this is empty the UI renders listings at
# their opening price but every trade is inert — there is no contract to call.
VITE_MARKET_ADDRESS=

# --- Server-side secrets (NOT here) ------------------------------------------
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY  bypasses RLS entirely. Supabase Edge Function
#                            secrets + your shell when seeding. Never in a
#                            VITE_ var, never committed.
# ROBINHOOD_RPC_URL          Edge Function secret (same URL, no VITE_ prefix).
# MARKET_ADDRESS             Edge Function secret (same address, no prefix).
# MARKET_DEPLOY_BLOCK        first block the indexer scans; skips dead history.
# ORACLE_AUTHORITY_PRIVATE_KEY  signs updatePrice. Oracle host only.
# DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY / ADMIN_PRIVATE_KEY  deploy + createListing. Local only.
#
# Keep ADMIN and ORACLE_AUTHORITY as separate keys from each other and from the
# deployer — the contract separates those privileges on purpose, and reusing
# one key collapses that separation back into a single point of compromise.

# --- Oracle service (oracle/run.ts) ------------------------------------------
# These belong on the oracle host, not in the app build.
#
# BLOCKSCOUT_API_KEY   free from Blockscout. Raises the request ceiling roughly
#                      4x; without it every cycle is slower but still correct.
# CYCLE_SECONDS        pause BETWEEN cycles, default 30. Not a period — the
#                      next cycle starts this long after the last one ended, so
#                      a slow cycle delays the next rather than overlapping it.
# PUSH_ONCHAIN         "0" to index and publish without signing anything. Run a
#                      staging copy this way and it needs no oracle key at all.
# ROBINHOOD_NETWORK    "mainnet" for chain 4663, otherwise testnet (46630).
